@[expose] public section

/-! # Identifying the Boolean ultrapower of `Erdos1172LevyCohen.Algebra κ` and `anonymousAlgebra κ`

Using the canonical two-stage string-condition preorder `Erdos1172Shioya.CohenCover.Condition θ (FirstAlgebra θ)`,
we give an abstract criterion (`realizeIso`) identifying any complete Boolean algebra `W` generated by an
injective `FirstAlgebra θ` embedding and a `θ`-indexed family of independent binary decisions with
`Completion (CohenCover.Condition θ (FirstAlgebra θ))`.

Applying this criterion both to `Erdos1172LevyCohen.Algebra θ` and to the Boolean ultrapower
`Erdos1172BooleanUltrapower.Algebra U (Erdos1172LevyCohen.Algebra κ)` under a `(κ, θ)`-fine normal
ultrafilter `U` yields the canonical isomorphism `levyCohenUltrapowerIso`. Because `Erdos1172LevyCohen.Algebra κ`
has a `≤ κ`-sized dense presentation (`exists_dense_presentation κ hκ`), `anonymousAlgebra κ` equals the
range of `≤ κ`-ary Boolean terms `AnonTerm κ`; well-founded induction along `EventuallySubterm U` together
with `value_fine_iSup` restricts `levyCohenUltrapowerIso` to a complete Boolean homomorphism
`anonymousUltrapowerHom : CompleteLatticeHom (Algebra U (anonymousAlgebra κ)) (anonymousAlgebra θ)`
sending `boundedAnonName U a (fun _ => anonymousSubset κ)` to `anonymousSubset θ`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 800000
noncomputable section
